    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter August 31st with a high-ceiling core, led by **Junior Caminero** (76.88) and **Trea Turner** (72.88). **Junior Caminero** is our premier play, benefiting from a massive 19% boost due to the favorable 4.92 xERA of the opposing starter, allowing him to capitalize on his elite power potential from the #3 spot. **Trea Turner** remains the engine of our stolen base strategy; while facing a mid-tier arm, his ability to manipulate the basepaths against a pitcher with a slow delivery provides an optimal environment for speed production. We are also leaning heavily into our lead-off options, with **Kyle Schwarber** (69.43), **Christian Yelich** (68.87), and **Hector Rodriguez** (65.93) all providing strong efficiency scores, bolstered by positive park factors and favorable lineup placement.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was bypassing **Carson Benge** (33.26), who fell short of our 40.0 floor. While his upside is enticing, the combination of a tough left-handed starter and unfavorable park conditions neutralized his projection, forcing him to the bench in favor of higher-floor assets. Conversely, we must monitor **Lars Nootbaar** (60.26) closely; his score assumes a lead-off assignment, and any shift in the official lineup could see his efficiency volatility increase. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (47.70) remains active, he carries significant risk; the opposing starter\u2019s elite 3.07 xERA and a harsh platoon disadvantage for a left-handed hitter significantly cap his value today, leaving him as a fringe play that we are keeping in the lineup primarily to chase a stolen base opportunity if the wind conditions at the park hold steady.",
